    "title": "WHO 5th grading & mitotic / Ki-67 assessment (GI NET)",
    "intro": "Assign the higher grade whenever mitotic rate and Ki-67 index fall into different tiers. Count mitoses in 10 mm2 (divide by 5 for mitoses per 2 mm2); count >= 500 tumour cells in the Ki-67 hot spot.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "WHO 5th Grade Cutoffs (GI NET G1–G3)",
      "points": [
       "G1: < 2 mitoses / 2 mm2 AND Ki-67 < 3%.",
       "G2: 2–20 mitoses / 2 mm2 OR Ki-67 3–20%.",
       "G3: > 20 mitoses / 2 mm2 OR Ki-67 > 20% with retained well-differentiated organoid morphology (distinguish from poorly differentiated NEC)."
      ],
